          <div class="faq-list">
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Premier Protein as good as Optimum Nutrition?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  On the label, nearly. Both powders are isolate-led whey blends with about 5 calories per gram of protein and 1 g of sugar. Gold Standard pulls ahead on certification, since its core flavors are NSF Certified for Sport and Premier publishes none, and on price per gram in the 5 lb tub. Premier wins on soy-free status and a 30 g one-step serving.
